<h3>Battalions</h3>

<p>Battalions are organized groups within Bloodhorde that are determined to
spread evil throughout the lands of Norrath. The role of battalions is to
provide order and structure for groups of similarly experienced members and
organize hunts for those members. </p>

<p>Bloodhorde has three Battalions: </p>

<ul type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><a href="Roster/blood_fist.asp">Blood
     Fist Battalion (lvls 24-34)</a> </li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><a href="Roster/bone_crush.asp">Bone
     Crush Battalion (lvls 35-46)</a> </li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><a href="Roster/black_venom.asp">Black
     Venom Battalion (lvls 47+)</a> </li>
</ul>

<p>Each battalion is lead by a Dragoon and Crusader (see <a
href="roles.htm">Guild
Roles</a> for more info on Dragoon and Crusader) that are of the level range
for their battalion, as the leaders are expected to hunt with their battalion. </p>

<p>The Dragoon and Crusader are responsible for choosing their Battalion's
weekly hunting spot. Specifying where the battalion will be hunting for at
least the next week gives the members the knowledge that when they log on, they
have a good chance of finding fellow Bloodhorde members that they can group
with. The Dragoon and Crusader can choose to move the hunting spot whenever
they wish, but they are strongly encouraged to keep the hunting spot in the
same place for at least one week. </p>

<p>It is strongly recommended that a hunt start on Sunday and run through
saturday. The Dragoon/Crusader should choose the next hunting spot (if they
want to move to another area) and announce it by Thursday. The Battalion should
start hunting at the new spot on sunday. </p>

<p>All battalion members are <b>extremely</b> encouraged to be at the
designated hunting spot for their battalion for the entire week. You should not
be off soloing if your battalion could use you. We also recognize the fact that
you will need to buy food, run errands, maybe spend a day in EC selling/buying.
So, we have determined that Wednesdays and Saturdays are considered &quot;free
days&quot;. On those days you may feel free to do anything you like. However,
if you have nothing to do, it would be beneficial to yourself and to your
battalion if you would continue to hunt with them on those days. </p>

<p><b>Cross Battalion Hunting</b> </p>

<p>Battalions are organized by level. A higher level member of one battalion
could easily group with a lower level member of the next higher battalion.
Members in this situation are given the freedom to choose which battalion they
would like to hunt with. For example, a level 33 member of Blood Fist (24-34)
may be able to join the hunt with Bone Crush (35-46). If they wish to join the
other battalion for a hunt, that would be acceptable. However, if the character
falls more than 2 lvls below the other battalion's minimum, we ask that you do
not go hunt with the other battalion. We want to keep battalions together. We
don't want half of a battalion going off to hunt with another leaving behind a small
number of people they could be hunting with. </p>

<p><b>Hunting Spot Guidelines</b> </p>

<p>When the Dragoon and Crusader choose a hunting spot for their members, they
should keep a few things in mind: </p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Make sure the hunting spot is
     near other possible places close by for members of your battalion to hunt.
     There may be times where there may not be enough members on to form a
     group, or a member may not be able to get a group. You want to give them
     an alternative that is close by so they can quickly come back to the
     hunting spot if other members log on, or a spot in a group opens up. </li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Make sure the hunting spot
     does not ruin faction for anybody. Being an evil-only guild we probably
     don't have as much problem as other guilds, but there are still some
     places that may give bad faction for some people. Karnor's Castle,
     Kaesora, and Howeling Stones all give bad faction with the &quot;evil
     outpost&quot; in the Overthere. Also, hunting Freeport guards may ruin
     faction for members that have worked hard to get their faction up in those
     areas. </li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Try to choose a spot that is
     relatively close to a bindable spot for melee classes.</li>
</ol>

